# Phase 2: Synthetic Data Purge

## Overview
Remove or tag all synthetic/bootstrap data from calibration pipelines so the system knows it has ZERO real learning, not fake "35 resolved outcomes."

## Requirements
- Functional: All `source: "bootstrap_synthetic"` and `source: "bootstrap"` records excluded from calibration
- Functional: Brain-refresh weekly reports show true state: "0 real outcomes, system uncalibrated"
- Non-functional: Don't delete files — tag and exclude (preserve audit trail)

## Related Code Files
- Modify: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\data\calibration\brier-scores.jsonl` — tag synthetic entries
- Modify: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\data\calibration\revenue-outcomes.jsonl` — tag synthetic entries
- Modify: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\data\deals\deal-pipeline.json` — tag bootstrap entries
- Modify: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\.claude\skills\business\feedback_loop\auto-outcome-detector.py` — skip synthetic in calculations
- Modify: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\.claude\skills\business\transaction-layer\nui-hunter\scripts\bias-calibrator.py` — skip synthetic

## Implementation Steps

1. In `brier-scores.jsonl`: Add `"_synthetic": true` field to all entries where `verified_by == "brier_backfill"` AND no real outcome exists
   - Keep entries in file for audit trail
   - Script: read all lines, tag, rewrite

2. In `revenue-outcomes.jsonl`: Add `"_synthetic": true` to all entries where `source == "bootstrap_synthetic"`

3. In `deal-pipeline.json`: Add `"_synthetic": true` to all pipeline entries where `source == "bootstrap"`

4. In `auto-outcome-detector.py`: When calculating stats, filter out entries with `_synthetic: true`
   ```python
   verified_entries = [e for e in entries if e.get("brier") is not None and not e.get("_synthetic")]
   ```

5. In `bias-calibrator.py`: Same filter — skip synthetic entries in bias calculation

6. In brain-refresh scripts: Update summary output to show:
   ```
   Real outcomes: X | Synthetic (excluded): Y | Calibration status: UNCALIBRATED if X < 5
   ```

## Success Criteria
- [ ] `auto-outcome-detector.py` reports 0 real verified entries (not 35)
- [ ] `bias-calibrator.py` reports "insufficient_data" for ALL verdict classes (not just some)
- [ ] Brain-refresh weekly shows "UNCALIBRATED" status
- [ ] No synthetic data influences any calibration calculation
- [ ] Original data preserved with `_synthetic: true` tag

## Risk Assessment
- Risk: Some downstream script relies on having ≥5 entries to function → will degrade gracefully to "insufficient_data" status (already handles this case)
- Risk: brain-refresh cron breaks → test locally first with `--dry-run`
